# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Used for `go run .` / running the
# binary directly. Docker Compose uses its own bundled Redis and ignores this.
#
# All of these are optional. With none set, the limiter runs purely in-memory.

# --- Redis backend (shared counters across instances) ---------------------
#
# Option A: a full connection URL. Managed providers (Railway, Upstash,
# Render, …) give you one; the password (and TLS, for rediss://) is inside it.
# RL_REDIS=redis://default:PASSWORD@HOST:6379
#
# Option B: a plain address, with the password separate.
# RL_REDIS=localhost:6379
# RL_REDIS_PASSWORD=your-password
#
# The app also reads Railway's native names as fallbacks: REDIS_URL,
# REDIS_PASSWORD, REDISPASSWORD.

# --- Server / algorithm (also settable as flags) -------------------------
# RL_ADDR=:8080
# RL_ALGO=token-bucket        # or: sliding-window
